"""
ZX / AlphaTensor-style MCX synthesis demo.

Compared to the old version this code:

1. Never calls ``pyzx.extract_circuit``.  Phase gadgets are routed with a
   low-CNOT randomized Steiner-tree phase-polynomial router, so a
   4-phase-tensor proposal stays 4 T/T-dagger gates in QASM.
2. Distinguishes exact unitary equivalence from "relative phase is allowed".
   The default path uses the exact 7-T CCX decomposition.  The 4-T Margolus
   (RCCX) proposal is accepted only when ``ALLOW_RELATIVE_PHASE=1``.
3. Does not build or CP/ALS-factor a dense 2^N x 2^N matrix.  Graph work is
   limited to sparse ZX topology / local phase-gadget features.  A small
   dense matrix is used only for small-support verification of the loss term.
4. A tiny, trainable PyTorch Geometric GNN replaces the hard-coded 4-T
   proposal: it consumes graph node/edge features and emits discrete phase
   classes with a softmax (cross-entropy training).  The C^4X stress test
   routes the resulting phase layers and reports GRAY vs Steiner CX/depth.
5. Reports FTQC metrics (strict T-count, scheduled T-depth, CX-depth), uses
   T-depth as the routing/training objective, and provides a 5-8 qubit
   sliding-window partitioner for large SVP-like phase-polynomial graphs.
"""

